# Documentation Sync

Every plan for a new feature or in-progress feature must include a documentation sync item.

When a change affects user-facing behavior, setup, architecture, schema, screenshots, or feature status, update the relevant documentation in the same branch:

- `README.md` for public-facing overview and high-level status.
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` for planned milestones and feature status changes.
- `docs/TECHNICAL_OVERVIEW.md` for architecture, data flow, or code-structure changes.
- `docs/SETUP.md` for build, secrets, SDK, Supabase, or CI setup changes.
- `docs/supabase/` for database schema and migration changes.
- Demo screenshots or GIFs when a visible app flow changes.

If no documentation update is needed, state that explicitly in the plan or summary.

## Status Labels

- `Planned`: work is not implemented yet.
- `In progress`: implementation exists but needs more behavior, tests, polish, or docs.
- `Done`: implementation, verification, and documentation are complete for the intended scope.
- `Paused`: work started but is intentionally not active.
